Yep.  It's very possible that the Dev Team seriously overestimated the
effects of level drain, given that there are so many ways to gain levels
and restore levels available to the player.  It's also possible that the
Dev Team underestimated how unwilling players would be to actually fight
their way to levels beyond 13 or so; I know I personally always hang
onto a couple gain level potions _or_ lure wraiths from the Valley of
the Dead in order to make level 14, rather than try to kill my way
through the exponentially-increasing XP.

And, of course, with such techniques available, why would anyone make
level 14 (or beyond) "the old way"?

